-- Q4440: Independence [hard/L4]
-- Issues: #3
UPDATE questions SET
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (B): Under the AICPA Code''s conceptual framework, close relatives (parents, siblings, non-dependent children) are not subject to the same bright-line rules as immediate family. However, a close relative''s material financial interest may still create threats to independence that must be evaluated under the conceptual framework to determine if safeguards can reduce the threat to an acceptable level.
Wrong (A): The AICPA Code does not exempt close relatives entirely. While they are not treated identically to immediate family, their financial interests still require evaluation under the conceptual framework.
Wrong (C): Independence is not automatically impaired by a close relative''s financial interest. The conceptual framework requires a threat evaluation rather than imposing an absolute prohibition.
Wrong (D): The relevant inquiry is whether the interest creates an unacceptable threat, not whether the relative is willing to divest. Divestiture may be a safeguard but is not the initial evaluation step.$EXPL$
