-- Q4444: Independence [medium/L2]
-- Issues: #3
UPDATE questions SET
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (D): Under the AICPA Code, when a covered member becomes aware of an independence impairment, she should promptly evaluate whether safeguards can reduce the threat to an acceptable level. If safeguards are insufficient, the member should resign from the engagement. The spousal stock ownership creates a direct financial interest requiring immediate action.
Wrong (A): Immediately withdrawing without evaluation is premature. The Code requires assessing whether safeguards (such as the spouse disposing of the interest) can restore independence before resignation.
Wrong (B): Notifying the SEC is not the first required step. The member''s initial obligation is to evaluate whether the impairment can be resolved through appropriate safeguards.
Wrong (C): Continuing the engagement while independence is impaired violates the AICPA Code. Disclosure in the audit report does not cure an independence impairment.$EXPL$
