-- Q4445: Independence [hard/L2]
-- Issues: #3
UPDATE questions SET
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (D): Under the AICPA Code, if a former engagement team member joins the client during the period covered by the financial statements being audited, independence may be impaired. The firm must evaluate whether the former member''s knowledge of the audit plan and procedures could compromise audit effectiveness, as required by the employment with audit client provisions.
Wrong (A): The position title or whether it is a key position is not the sole determinant. The critical factor is that the individual was on the engagement team during the covered period.
Wrong (B): Influence over accounting matters is relevant but not the only consideration. Knowledge of the audit approach itself can compromise independence.
