-- Q4451: Professional Skepticism and Judgment [medium/L2]
-- Issues: #3
UPDATE questions SET
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (C): Developing an independent expectation and comparing it to management''s estimate demonstrates professional skepticism by not simply accepting management''s figures at face value. Under AU-C 540, this approach allows the auditor to assess the reasonableness of the estimate and identify potential biases or errors in management''s assumptions.
Wrong (A): Accepting the estimate based on past reliability fails to exercise skepticism. Prior accuracy does not guarantee current period estimates are reasonable.
Wrong (B): Using the same estimate as the prior year without evaluation ignores changes in conditions and fails to critically assess the current period''s circumstances.
Wrong (D): Relying solely on management''s specialist without further procedures fails to exercise skepticism. The auditor must evaluate the specialist''s work and assess its appropriateness.$EXPL$
