-- Q4452: Professional Skepticism and Judgment [medium/L2]
-- Issues: #3
UPDATE questions SET
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (C): Under AU-C 230, documenting professional judgments provides a record of the basis for the auditor''s conclusions and the rationale for decisions made throughout the audit. This enables engagement quality reviewers, peer reviewers, and regulatory inspectors to understand the auditor''s reasoning and assess whether sufficient appropriate evidence was obtained.
Wrong (A): Documentation serves broader purposes than legal compliance. Its primary role is to support the auditor''s conclusions and facilitate quality review, not merely to satisfy legal requirements.
Wrong (B): Documentation is not created to be used against the auditor. Its purpose is to demonstrate the basis for professional judgments and support the audit opinion.
