-- Q4455: Professional Skepticism and Judgment [hard/L2]
-- Issues: #3
UPDATE questions SET
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (A): Automation bias occurs when auditors place excessive trust in the outputs of automated tools or data analytics without applying sufficient professional skepticism. Under AU-C 200, auditors must critically assess all evidence, including automated outputs, to evaluate whether results are reasonable and the underlying data is reliable.
Wrong (B): Automation bias is the opposite of preferring manual procedures. It describes over-reliance on automated tools, not resistance to them.
Wrong (C): Management''s preference for automated accounting systems is an operational choice unrelated to auditor bias in evaluating automated audit tool outputs.
Wrong (D): Using computer-assisted audit techniques in all engagements describes a methodology choice, not a cognitive bias. The bias arises from uncritical acceptance of outputs, not from using the tools.$EXPL$
