-- Q4457: Professional Skepticism and Judgment [easy/L2]
-- Issues: #3
UPDATE questions SET
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (C): Under AU-C 200 and AU-C 500, professional judgment requires the auditor to consider both the sufficiency (quantity) and appropriateness (quality, including relevance and reliability) of audit evidence. Neither dimension alone is adequate—the auditor must assess both to determine whether enough evidence of the right quality has been obtained.
Wrong (A): Considering only quantitative factors ignores qualitative aspects such as the nature of misstatements and the reliability of evidence sources, which are equally important.
Wrong (B): Considering only qualitative factors ignores the need for adequate volume of evidence. Quality without sufficient quantity is incomplete.
Wrong (D): Audit committee preferences do not dictate the auditor''s professional judgment about evidence. The auditor independently determines what evidence is needed.$EXPL$
