-- Q4458: Professional Skepticism and Judgment [medium/L3]
-- Issues: #3
UPDATE questions SET
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (D): Under AU-C 500, when contradictory evidence is discovered, the auditor should reconsider the reliability of other audit evidence obtained and perform additional procedures to resolve the inconsistency. A $340,000 discrepancy between a bank confirmation and management''s reconciliation may indicate the originally obtained evidence is less reliable than assessed.
Wrong (A): Ignoring contradictory evidence, even for immaterial accounts, violates professional skepticism. The discrepancy may signal broader reliability issues or fraud indicators requiring investigation.
Wrong (B): Withdrawing from the engagement is premature. The auditor should first investigate the discrepancy and attempt to resolve it through additional procedures.
