-- Q4459: Professional Skepticism and Judgment [hard/L4]
-- Issues: #3
UPDATE questions SET
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (D): Under AU-C 200, professional judgment requires evaluating whether accounting treatments reflect the economic substance of transactions rather than merely their legal form. In related-party transactions with no cash consideration and seller financing, the legal structure may differ from economic reality, and the auditor must assess whether the applicable framework''s requirements are properly applied based on substance.
Wrong (A): Matching industry treatment is not the standard. The appropriate accounting treatment depends on the specific transaction''s substance under the applicable financial reporting framework, not peer comparison.
Wrong (B): Selecting the treatment that maximizes net income is contrary to faithful representation. The goal is accurate portrayal of economic substance, not income optimization.
Wrong (C): Conservatism is not the overriding objective. The auditor evaluates whether the treatment faithfully represents the transaction''s substance, which may or may not be the most conservative option.$EXPL$
