-- Q4460: Professional Skepticism and Judgment [hard/L2]
-- Issues: #3
UPDATE questions SET
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (D): Under AU-C 200, presumptive doubt means the auditor should not be satisfied with less-than-persuasive evidence when more persuasive evidence could reasonably be obtained. It requires maintaining a critical mindset that demands sufficient appropriate evidence before drawing conclusions, without presuming dishonesty or fraud.
Wrong (A): Professional skepticism does not require refusing all audit evidence. The auditor must evaluate evidence critically, not reject it categorically.
Wrong (B): Presuming all management representations are false goes beyond skepticism into distrust. The standard requires neither believing nor disbelieving management''s claims without corroboration.
Wrong (C): Assuming fraud exists until proven otherwise overstates the standard. AU-C 200 requires a questioning mindset, not a presumption of fraud.$EXPL$
