-- Issues: #3
UPDATE questions SET
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (C): Journal entries posted near year-end without adequate supporting documentation are a common fraud risk indicator. Under AU-C 240, professional skepticism requires investigating such entries further because they may represent fictitious transactions or management override of controls. Testing journal entries is a specifically required fraud risk procedure.
Wrong (A): Accepting entries based solely on a verbal explanation fails to exercise professional skepticism. Verbal explanations without corroborating documentation are insufficient for unusual entries.
