-- Q4466: Terms of Engagement [easy/L1]
-- Issues: #3
UPDATE questions SET
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (A): Under AU-C 210, an engagement letter must include the identification of the applicable financial reporting framework, management''s responsibility for preparation of the financial statements, the objective and scope of the audit, and the auditor''s responsibilities. These are required elements ensuring mutual understanding of the engagement.
Wrong (B): The names of all staff members are not a required element. Staffing decisions are operational matters that may change during the engagement and need not be specified in the letter.
Wrong (C): An engagement letter cannot guarantee detection of all fraud. AU-C 210 requires the letter to describe inherent limitations of an audit, not to offer guarantees.
Wrong (D): Specific audit procedures are not required in the engagement letter. The auditor determines procedures based on professional judgment during the engagement, not in advance.$EXPL$
