-- Q4475: Terms of Engagement [hard/L2]
-- Issues: #3
UPDATE questions SET
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (A): Under AU-C 210, if management imposes a scope limitation as a condition of the engagement that would result in a disclaimer of opinion, the auditor should ordinarily not accept such a limited engagement unless required by law or regulation. Accepting an engagement designed to produce a disclaimer does not serve the interests of financial statement users.
Wrong (B): Simply accepting and issuing a disclaimer is inappropriate when the scope limitation is imposed as a precondition. The auditor should refuse the terms rather than accept a fundamentally limited engagement.
Wrong (C): Negotiating a higher fee does not address the scope limitation problem. The issue is the inability to perform sufficient audit work, not the compensation level.
Wrong (D): A qualified opinion is issued for less pervasive scope limitations. When the limitation is so severe as to require a disclaimer, accepting the engagement on those terms is inappropriate.$EXPL$
